# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the Swift evaluation window (tp4/swift; scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/swift and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN, ONE TAG AT A TIME (wait for the run to finish; never cancel a running card job).
# Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a registry: the cards are resolved at run time. The jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed from the branch by its author. ORDER.txt has the
# order, the stop rules, the minutes and the read rules.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-swift-1 is a PLACEHOLDER for the tag B0 builds from the pushed branch head WITH the K64j-OQ graft (sed -i 's/tp4-swift-1/<tag>/' *.env). A commit of a file
# the image carries needs a new B0 build and a new tag in every template. This window never stops, starts or hands back the node agent.
# C2_MODEL_REPO / C2_MODEL_REVISION (qwen_c2_checkpoint.py): a job that carries them serves the Swift checkpoint with its own converted-weight directory (never the base's); a job without them is the base,
# byte for byte what production serves.
# W0 (STOP): the FIRST BOOT of Swift, which builds its converted-weight cache. The cache is keyed by the checkpoint (TT_CACHE_PATH becomes <base
# path>-ckpt/<repo>--<revision>), so it starts EMPTY: every tensor is converted from the checkpoint's safetensors (bf16 to the TP4 shards in bfp8 and bfp4, the packed MLP
# blocks) and written, then the engines are built and the traces captured. The base's cache is neither read nor written. EVIDENCE for the time: the base's whole four-card
# converted cache (1,246 tensor files, 24 GB, in tensor_cache_bfp8 and tensor_cache_bfp8_mesh1x4) carries file times within 3 minutes 15 seconds of each other, so the
# conversion and write are about 3 to 4 minutes; add the first read of the 52 GB of safetensors from a cold page cache (minutes) and the warm boot (3 to 14 minutes by
# load): ESTIMATE 8 to 25 minutes for the first boot (the cold general-path TP4 boot of the first four-card run was ready after 376 s). The Swift cache is about as large as
# the base's, 24 GB. The BOX is 150 minutes and the smoke step's own readiness wait is 80 minutes: a boot killed during the write leaves a partial cache directory and the
# next boot then logs "its first boot never completed" for it (delete <hub>/.qwen-c2/weights-ckpt/<key> and re-run W0). RUN WITH THE CI PAUSED (a model load under CI load
# has hit the platform's load timeout). Tests: warmup, coding (a Python rewrite of a shell script) and concurrent8_steady (the smoke check requires it on this profile): a
# coding answer and the first multi-user rounds on the new weights. THE SAME FILE IS THE PRODUCTION FIRST BOOT: run right after production is unloaded, it builds the cache
# the platform's boot will find (the platform container mounts the same hub, so the keyed directory under /experiment-cache, a link into the hub, is the same files). READ:
# CHECKPOINT READ (the workflow passes c2_smoke_check.py --expect-checkpoint): the container log holds "[QWEN-C2] checkpoint
# ukisai/Swift-1.5-Qwen3.8-27b@b4c84d42903a8646b25857eb2827288d92ed85a4 key=... weight_cache=.../weights-ckpt/<key> base_cache=... (the base cache is not read or written)"
# once, a "weight cache ...: created|found" line, and the worker's "[QWEN-C2] checkpoint bound ..." line; the models answer names ukisai/Swift-1.5-Qwen3.8-27b. "ready=1
# after N s" in the step log: RECORD N, it is the cold load; the warm one is SW1's, and it is the number a production deploy of Swift has to fit under the platform's
# bounded load attempt (about 13.5 minutes). "[QWEN-C2] weight cache complete (first boot of this directory)" once. The octo rounds of concurrent8_steady, no stall, no
# "audit mismatch". Any refusal line ("cannot serve the asked checkpoint") means the snapshot is not the base's in config/tokenizer/template or is incomplete: read it, fix
# the download, do NOT work around it. TELEMETRY (C2_TELEMETRY=1, scripts/ci/card_telemetry.py): the read-only ARC sidecar samples every chip once a second through the
# smoke step; the first [TELEMETRY] line must say decode check ok. A rate difference that comes with a different loaded AICLK between the arms is the clocks, not the
# checkpoint. Duration (estimate): 60 minutes.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset smoke
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-swift-1
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-fx-traffic-s4
C2_MODEL_REPO=ukisai/Swift-1.5-Qwen3.8-27b
C2_MODEL_REVISION=b4c84d42903a8646b25857eb2827288d92ed85a4
C2_SMOKE_TESTS=warmup,coding,concurrent8_steady
C2_TELEMETRY=1
C2_BOX_MINUTES=150
